From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: media: cedrus: vc1: refuse pictures narrower than the hardware
 decodes

The hardware decodes VC-1 pictures narrower than 128 pixels wrongly or
not at all. The widths in the sequence and entry-point controls are
checked against that minimum, but the width programmed into the
hardware is the width of the OUTPUT format, halved for a
reduced-resolution (RESPIC) picture of a Simple or Main profile
MULTIRES sequence. The OUTPUT format can be as narrow as 16 pixels, and
a 128 to 255 pixel wide format gives a half width below the minimum, so
such a picture reached the hardware while the controls passed their
checks.

Refuse the request in cedrus_vc1_setup(), before the engine is enabled,
when the width that would be programmed is below the minimum.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus_vc1.c | 11 ++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus_vc1.c b/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus_vc1.c
index 1962c2047..18346c36c 100644
--- a/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus_vc1.c
+++ b/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus_vc1.c
@@ -565,6 +565,16 @@ static int cedrus_vc1_setup(struct cedrus_ctx *ctx, struct cedrus_run *run)
 	    vb2_get_plane_payload(src_buf, 0) > buf_size - CEDRUS_VC1_SRC_SLACK)
 		return -EINVAL;
 
+	/*
+	 * The hardware is given the width of the OUTPUT format, or half of it
+	 * for a reduced-resolution picture, whatever widths the controls
+	 * carry. Pictures narrower than CEDRUS_VC1_MIN_WIDTH decode wrongly
+	 * or not at all.
+	 */
+	cedrus_vc1_coded_size(ctx, run, &width, &height);
+	if (width < CEDRUS_VC1_MIN_WIDTH)
+		return -EINVAL;
+
 	/* Decoded bitplanes must fit in the bitplanes control. */
 	if (picture->bitplane_flags &&
 	    cedrus_vc1_bitplane_size(ctx, run) > V4L2_VC1_BITPLANE_SIZE)
@@ -885,7 +895,6 @@ static int cedrus_vc1_setup(struct cedrus_ctx *ctx, struct cedrus_run *run)
 
 	/* Set frame dimensions. */
 
-	cedrus_vc1_coded_size(ctx, run, &width, &height);
 	reg = VE_DEC_VC1_FSIZE_WIDTH(width);
 	reg |= VE_DEC_VC1_FSIZE_HEIGHT(height);
 	cedrus_write(dev, VE_DEC_VC1_FSIZE, reg);
